[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: SW-H1FWT-
TITLE: Design Items

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWT-28
TITLE: Communication Interface
STATEMENT: >>>
The timer firmware communicates with the main control application firmware. The timer firmware in
response reports the current remaining or elapsed time. This communication takes place using an
I2C bus. The firmware utilizes the timer MCU's built in I2C peripheral hardware instead of manually
'bit-banging' a set of general IO. The firmware sets up the timer MCU as an I2C slave device to the
main control MCU's master device.

At the board level of hardware, there are two timer MCUs which share a single I2C bus with the
main control MCU that acts as the master. Due to this, the two timer MCUs need to have different
I2C addresses. Instead of building and maintaining two versions of timer firmware, the two timer
MCUs instead have either a pull-up or pull-down resistor on one of their input pins. This pin value is
read at the start of firmware execution and is used to determine which slave address is used for the
specific MCU that the firmware is running on.

The firmware enables the I2C peripheral's data received interrupt, which allows an interrupt to be
processed whenever a data byte is received from the I2C master. Once a complete data packet is
received, per the application-level communication protocol, a flag is set so that synchronous packet
processing may be performed on the data.
<<<
