[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWT-31
TITLE: Output Signals
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware has one LED output control signal for debugging.

The firmware has one interlock fault output signal which can trigger to stop emission of the system.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWT-9
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWT-32
TITLE: Communication Protocol
STATEMENT: >>>
The communication data from the main control firmware are commands which are timer related
tasks. These commands are setting the target time, pausing the timer counting and resetting the
timer (including the interlock IO used to terminate emissions), as well as a report time request.
There is no start command, as start is performed via hardware IO. This is due to the two timer
MCUs sharing a single serial communication bus. To ensure that the timer counts are as
synchronized as possible, the trigger to start is instead done via a digital signal rather than
sequential serial commands. This signal only starts with the count of the timers and cannot stop
them.

The communication data to the main control firmware reports the time value being counted, as well
as the state of the timer.

Both received and sent messages use a simple checksum value to check the validity of the
message payloads
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWT-14
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWT-33
TITLE: Manufacturer Hardware Abstraction
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware integrates source code provided by the manufacturer of the microcontroller unit to
interface with various peripherals of the microcontroller. These include functions to interface with
the following peripherals of the microcontroller:

- I2C serial port
- GPIO
- Timer counter
<<<
